session-child: use _exit() in the signal handler

exit() is not async-signal-safe: if SIGTERM arrives while the main
thread holds the malloc lock, the atexit/destructor path deadlocks in
free() and session-child hangs until it is SIGKILLed, delaying logins.

https://github.com/canonical/lightdm/issues/484

--- a/src/session-child.c
+++ b/src/session-child.c
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ signal_cb (int signum)
     if (child_pid > 0)
         kill (child_pid, signum);
     else
-        exit (EXIT_SUCCESS);
+        _exit (EXIT_SUCCESS);
 }
 
 static XAuthority *
